# Store (Drizzle + node:sqlite)

- The schema is `src/db/schema.ts`. A schema change is a migration generated with drizzle-kit; never edit a
  generated migration by hand and never change the database outside a migration.
- Repositories (`store.reviews`, `store.findings`, …) are the only way the rest of the code touches the
  database. No raw SQL or Drizzle tables outside `packages/store`.
- Rows are mapped to schema types in `mappers.ts`; callers never see a row shape.
- Timestamps are integer milliseconds. Ids are time-ordered strings from `newId`.
- JSON columns are parsed with the zod schema from `@crit/schema` on read.
- Writes that must stay consistent go in one transaction.
- The cache and `events` tables are append-only logs for the review; do not rewrite history, add a new row.
